# Secrets. The build context is read from disk, not from git, so a developer's
# local .env is present here even though it is gitignored. Without these rules
# `COPY backend /repo/backend` would bake database and JWT secrets into an
# image layer. .env.example is a different filename and stays included.
.env
**/.env
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.venv
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
.git
.gitignore
ml/notebooks
ml/results
ml/data
docs
*.md
!README.md
!backend/README.md
